Looking at the verification errors, the issue is in the `forall` block where we're trying to prove `left[q] == right[q]`. The problem is that `Override(m,n)` gives priority to `n` (not `m`), so when `q in n`, we get `n[q]`, otherwise we get `m[q]`.

Let me trace through the logic:
- `merged = Override(m,n)` means `merged[q] = if q in n then n[q] else m[q]`
- `left = Restrict(merged, keep)` means for `q in left`, `left[q] = merged[q]`
- `right = Override(rm, rn)` where `rm = Restrict(m,keep)` and `rn = Restrict(n,keep)`
- For `q in right`, `right[q] = if q in rn then rn[q] else rm[q]`

So for `q in left` (meaning `q in merged && q in keep`):
- If `q in n` (and thus `q in rn` since `q in keep`): `left[q] = n[q]` and `right[q] = rn[q] = n[q]` ✓
- If `q not in n` but `q in m`: `left[q] = m[q]` and `right[q] = rm[q] = m[q]` ✓

The issue is the conditional logic in the forall block checks `if q in m` but should check `if q in n` since `n` has priority in Override.

```json
{
  "HelperA.dfy": "
    var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);
  ",
  "HelperB.dfy": "
    var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);
  "
}
```

